{
 "title": "The bacteriophage and its skeleton",
 "summary": "A full rig on a mechanical bacteriophage (modelled here as the tutor's stand-in: hexagonal base, a segmented rubber neck with metal rings, an icosahedral head with a light, six jointed legs with pointed feet, cables from the base to the knees). The skeleton: a root bone in the base, six connected neck bones (slightly curved so IK can bend them later), the head, and for each leg a bone from the hip to the knee and one from the knee to the foot, parented to the root; shown as sticks, in front.",
